                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">Printers and peripherals</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold">Compatibility before installation</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-inverse-ink/70">
                        The exact printer, connection, primary device and available manufacturer software are checked. Wi-Fi, USB, print and scan functions are tested only where the equipment and current software support them.
                    </p>
                    <a href="/services/new-printer-setup-ivanhoe/" class="mt-5 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-bold text-accent underline">See new-printer setup</a>
                </article>

                <article class="rounded-3xl bg-inverse p-7 text-inverse-ink md:p-8 md:col-span-2">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">Privacy and security</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold">Practical layers, with limits explained</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-inverse-ink/70">
                        Updates, multi-factor authentication, strong unique credentials, backups and appropriate privacy settings are useful foundations. Encrypted email, a VPN or other privacy software may help with a specific need, but no single product makes a device, account or connection anonymous or completely secure.
                    </p>
                    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
                        <a href="/services/scam-security-help-ivanhoe/" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-bold text-accent underline">See scam and account-security help</a>
